# RENDERED OUTPUT, at any depth. `experiments/*/renders/` missed
# `experiments/007-frameworks/three-vanilla/renders/` by one path segment, and
# the untracked tree held 284 MB of video and synthesised speech under paths
# like that. Every one of them is regenerable by a command in the sibling
# README, and where a render is EVIDENCE the writeup cites it by path and says
# how to remake it — which is the durable record, not the bytes. Anything that
# genuinely must ship is force-added.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mp3
*.wav
.*.mp4.parts/
experiments/**/audio/
experiments/**/deck/
experiments/**/deck-*/
experiments/**/out/

# built demo output — regenerate with `npm run demo`
demo/deck/

# synthesised speech — regenerate with `decksmith narrate`. Content-addressed,
# so re-running it after an edit re-speaks only the sentences that moved.
demo/audio/
*.deck

# Test scratch that lands HERE rather than in /tmp. `mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), …))`
# resolves against TMPDIR, and some sandboxes point TMPDIR at the working
# directory — which put 335 of these in the tree before anyone noticed. Ignored
# rather than fixed in the tests: on a machine with a normal TMPDIR they are
# already in /var/folders and the OS reaps them.
#
# THE LIST HAS TO BE COMPLETE OR IT IS WORSE THAN NOTHING. It covered three of
# the seven prefixes, so 2333 directories accumulated and `git add -A` swept 14
# files out of four of them into four separate commits — an MCP upload fixture,
# a storyboard schema and two pairs of verify frames, none of which anything
# reads. Every prefix any of these mkdtemp calls uses belongs here.
decksmith-narrate-*/
decksmith-pack-*/
decksmith-plan-*/
decksmith-server-*/
ds-mcp-*/
ds-prov-*/
hf-*/
node-compile-cache/
tsx-*/
.scratch/

# One-off probe output from investigations whose durable record is .planning/.
